<item>
            <title>[LU-20901] sanity test_0e test_3: EIO after spurious MDT0000-osp-MDT0002 eviction at startup</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20901</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;sanity test_0e and test_3 both FAIL with &quot;Input/output error&quot; moments&lt;br/&gt;
after the review-dne-selinux-ssk-part-1 cluster finishes setup.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;trevis-156vm29 (hosting both lustre-MDT0000 and lustre-MDT0002) logs,&lt;br/&gt;
at the exact second test_0e starts:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;  Lustre: lustre-MDT0000: Received MDS connection from 10.240.46.120@tcp,&lt;br/&gt;
    removing former export from 0@lo&lt;br/&gt;
  Lustre: lustre-MDT0000-lwp-MDT0002: Connection to lustre-MDT0000&lt;br/&gt;
    (at 0@lo) was lost; in progress operations using this service will&lt;br/&gt;
    wait for recovery to complete&lt;br/&gt;
  LustreError: lustre-MDT0000-osp-MDT0002: This client was evicted by&lt;br/&gt;
    lustre-MDT0000; in progress operations using this service will fail.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;followed moments later by:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;  Lustre: lustre-MDT0000: already connected client&lt;br/&gt;
    lustre-MDT0000-lwp-OST0000_UUID (at 10.240.46.130@tcp) with handle&lt;br/&gt;
    ...  Rejecting client with the same UUID trying to reconnect with&lt;br/&gt;
    handle ...&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;test_0e&apos;s rmdir and test_3&apos;s &quot;lfs mkdir -i3&quot; both need the co-located&lt;br/&gt;
MDT0000/MDT0002 OSP, which this eviction just dropped, and both return&lt;br/&gt;
EIO in that window.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The eviction path is ldlm_lib.c&apos;s generic &quot;removing former export&quot;&lt;br/&gt;
connection-replace logic when a client reconnects from a different NID&lt;br/&gt;
than its existing export used; it is not part of this patch&apos;s diff&lt;br/&gt;
(lustre/mgs, lustre/target/tgt_mount.c and lustre/mgc changes on this&lt;br/&gt;
change are about MGS-bit reporting over nidtbl, not export or LWP/OSP&lt;br/&gt;
connection handling). test_0e and test_3 both have sporadic failures&lt;br/&gt;
on unrelated changes in the last 30 days with no shared feature, which&lt;br/&gt;
points to a pre-existing startup race when several targets mount and&lt;br/&gt;
reconnect in quick succession on a shared node, not something this&lt;br/&gt;
patch introduces.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Maloo session: &lt;a href=&quot;https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sessions/1833010c-bd1f-4fed-a786-e11c81cb855f&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sessions/1833010c-bd1f-4fed-a786-e11c81cb855f&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
Test set: &lt;a href=&quot;https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/2c251607-6aa8-4c8f-9b1f-debff4d06b7e&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/2c251607-6aa8-4c8f-9b1f-debff4d06b7e&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Raised by Patch Watcher run pw-engineer-68474-ps10-dfc3aca5a570 on &lt;a href=&quot;https://review.whamcloud.com/68474&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://review.whamcloud.com/68474&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
